## Top 5

1. **Purview retention for Copilot memory (GA):** Copilot memory items live in a hidden Exchange mailbox folder and have had no retention story until now. GA in this roadmap item closes that gap, giving admins versioning and preservation controls for inactive memory items - a prerequisite for defensible Copilot governance in regulated environments.

2. **DSI launch from endpoint DLP alerts (Preview):** Analysts can now pivot directly from an endpoint DLP alert into Data Security Investigations, automatically pulling the files that triggered the alert. This cuts the manual correlation step out of exfiltration investigations and tightens the response loop considerably.

3. **Organizational Messages support for Hybrid-joined devices (Preview):** If you have been holding back on Organizational Messages because your fleet is hybrid-joined rather than Entra-native, this removes that blocker. Hybrid support is now in preview with GA targeted for June 2026.

4. **Lifecycle Workflows cloning now documented:** Microsoft has published guidance on cloning existing Lifecycle Workflows, which meaningfully reduces the overhead of maintaining parallel onboarding and offboarding workflow variants across business units or regions.

5. **Global Secure Access macOS client documentation reapplied:** Updated GSA macOS client docs re-landed this week after an earlier revert. If you are planning or running a macOS GSA rollout, verify your deployment guidance is sourced from the current article revision.

## Security & Compliance

- **[Reminder: Ask Microsoft Anything with David Weston (8/25 at 8AM PST)](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/microsoft-security-community/reminder-ask-microsoft-anything-with-david-weston-is-tomorrow-8/ba-p/4549690)** [GA] - David Weston, who leads Agentic Security at Microsoft, hosted an AMA covering AI-driven defense, frontier security model training, and autonomous defender agents. The session recording is worth tracking down if your team is evaluating agentic security tooling or AI-assisted vulnerability discovery; Weston's team is building the underlying systems that will shape how these capabilities surface in Defender products.

- **[Microsoft Purview: Data Security Investigations - analyze files tied to endpoint DLP alerts](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=558547)** [Preview] - Currently in preview with GA targeted for September 2026, this feature lets you launch a DSI investigation directly from an endpoint DLP alert and automatically collect the relevant files for review. This removes the manual correlation step between DLP alerting and content analysis, which is particularly valuable when investigating large-scale exfiltration events with many triggered alerts across multiple users and endpoints.

- **[Microsoft 365 admin center: Organizational Messages now supports Hybrid-joined Devices](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=503564)** [Preview] - Hybrid-joined device support for Organizational Messages is now in preview, with GA expected June 2026. Organizations that standardized on hybrid join and previously had to exclude those endpoints from messaging campaigns can now close that coverage gap; validate that your existing message targeting configurations will behave as expected when the feature reaches GA.

- **[Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management - Retention for Copilot Memory](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=569612)** [GA] - Retention policies can now target Copilot memory items stored in users' Exchange mailboxes, including both explicitly saved memories and inferences derived from chat history. Admins gain versioning and preservation controls over inactive memory items, while active memory remains under Copilot's own management. If your organization has Copilot deployed in a regulated environment, treat this as a required governance control to evaluate and configure now.

## Action Required

There are no CVEs and no hard-deadline items in this week's digest. The following items most warrant your attention in the next 30 days:

- **[Purview Retention for Copilot Memory](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=569612)** [GA] - Now GA. If Copilot is deployed in a regulated or eDiscovery-sensitive environment, evaluate and configure retention policies for Exchange-hosted Copilot memory items before users accumulate significant memory history with no preservation controls in place.

- **[DSI Launch from Endpoint DLP Alerts](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=558547)** [Preview] - GA is September 2026. Enroll in preview now to validate how DSI integrates with your existing endpoint DLP policy set and alert workflows before the feature rolls broadly; early testing will also inform any SOC runbook updates needed at GA.

- **[Organizational Messages for Hybrid-joined Devices](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=503564)** [Preview] - GA targeted June 2026. If your fleet is predominantly hybrid-joined, test current preview behavior against your targeting rules and confirm that message scope aligns with your intended audience before GA rollout.

## Documentation Updates

**Identity & Access**

- **[New article: SAMAccountName attribute in Entra ID](https://github.com/MicrosoftDocs/entra-docs/commit/58c21f91283136b2713d310cf3c810d3ee6a7e9f)** - A new article covering the SAMAccountName attribute in Entra ID context has been published, useful for teams managing hybrid identity scenarios where legacy attribute dependencies matter.

- **[Global Secure Access macOS client docs reapplied](https://github.com/MicrosoftDocs/entra-docs/commit/81ba8429e11ab2c73d9f890ced41c193e1bcf7b4)** - Previously reverted GSA macOS client documentation updates have been re-landed; if you are deploying or troubleshooting the GSA client on macOS, source guidance from the current revision of this article.

- **[Lifecycle Workflows: cloning an existing workflow](https://github.com/MicrosoftDocs/entra-docs/commit/ecd837b3898d4fd03bc8f320b0013b41a8fe10e5)** - New guidance documents how to clone an existing Lifecycle Workflow, reducing the effort of maintaining parallel workflow variants for different departments or regions.

- **[Lifecycle Workflows: relative time-based triggers now documented](https://github.com/MicrosoftDocs/entra-docs/commit/2f521761794eb9f4eb0da671db264906dd841883)** - Documentation for relative time-based workflow triggers has been published, with the preview offset limit set to 365 days; relevant for teams building joiner/leaver workflows that fire relative to an attribute date rather than a fixed schedule.

**Endpoint & Device Management**

- **[Defender catch-up scan behavior updates](https://github.com/MicrosoftDocs/memdocs/commit/439f9830c3d3114e08646bcb25286bece432895c)** - Documentation covering Defender catch-up scan behavior has been updated; review if you manage scan scheduling policies in Intune to ensure your configured behavior aligns with current product guidance.